.TH "tm" "1" "2026\-10\-27"
.PP
.SH NAME
tm \- universal taskmark utility
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtm\fR <command> [options]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBtm\fR is the command\-line interface for SPEC\-TASKMARK\-03 taskmark files.\& It
provides subcommands to sweep completed tasks between task documents, rotate
sprints, archive aged\-out sections, validate files for spec compliance, and
filter arbitrary text into and out of a payload block.\& The specification it
implements is documented in \fIdoc/taskmark_spec.\&md\fR.\&
.PP
Unless a path is given, \fBtm\fR operates on the \fIdoc/tasks\fR directory relative to
the current working directory (the layout described by the spec).\&
.PP
.SH COMMANDS
\fBinit\fR
.RS 4
Bootstrap \fIdoc/tasks\fR with starter \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR, \fIfuture.\&tm.\&md\fR, and
\fIcompleted.\&tm.\&md\fR files.\& Never overwrites a file that already exists.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBsweep\fR
.RS 4
Move every `\- [x]` task and its payload out of \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR and into
\fIcompleted.\&tm.\&md\fR, under a "## Sprint <sprint>" heading matching
\fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR'\&s current \fBsprint\fR field (appending into that section if
it is already the most recent one, rather than duplicating it).\&
Headings and top\-level prose are never swept, even when every task
beneath them is done.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBrotate\fR
.RS 4
A sweep, then update \fBsprint\fR and \fBdate\fR in \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR'\&s
frontmatter and \fBdate\fR in \fIcompleted.\&tm.\&md\fR'\&s.\& Requires \fB\-\-sprint\fR.\&
\fIfuture.\&tm.\&md\fR is never read or written, and no task is ever promoted
automatically.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBarchive\fR
.RS 4
Move sections aged out of \fIcompleted.\&tm.\&md\fR into
\fIdoc/tasks/archive/<YYYY>/<YYYY\-MM>.\&tm.\&md\fR, grouped by the month of
each section'\&s most recent \fBCompleted\fR task.\& A section is retained if
it is among the 10 newest or its most recent \fBCompleted\fR task is dated
within the last 14 days.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBvalidate\fR [\-\-fix] [file.\&.\&.\&]
.RS 4
Validate taskmark file(s) for SPEC\-TASKMARK\-03 compliance.\& If no \fIfile\fR
is given, defaults to the configured active file.\& If \fB\-\-fix\fR is given,
automatically repairs common formatting errors (over\-indented bullet
continuations and sub\-lists, wrapped labeled fields, missing blank lines
after labeled fields, hard tabs, and top\-level dash bullets converted
to '\&*'\&).\& Exits 0 on success (or successful repair), 1 on validation
failure or file error.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBindent\fR [info]
.RS 4
Read stdin, prefix every non\-blank line with the four\-space payload
indent, and write the result to stdout.\& Blank lines are emitted
genuinely empty.\& \fIinfo\fR, if given, wraps the result in a fenced code
block carrying that info string.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdedent\fR [\-\-fence]
.RS 4
Read stdin, remove exactly four leading spaces from every non\-blank
line, and write the result to stdout.\& Exits non\-zero rather than
truncate a line that lacks the full four\-space prefix.\& \fB\-\-fence\fR also
drops the first and last line, for lifting a fenced block back out.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBhelp\fR
.RS 4
Show a short usage summary.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBversion\fR
.RS 4
Print the version and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
\fB\-\-sprint\fR \fIVALUE\fR
.RS 4
New sprint identifier to stamp on \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR.\& Required with
\fBrotate\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Report what would move and change nothing.\& Applies to \fBsweep\fR,
\fBrotate\fR, and \fBarchive\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-tasks\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Directory holding the task files.\& Defaults to \fI.\&/doc/tasks\fR, or the
\fBtasks_dir\fR set in \fI.\&taskmarkrc\fR (see CONFIGURATION).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Show help for the command.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH FILES
\fIdoc/tasks/active.\&tm.\&md\fR
.RS 4
The current sprint.\&
.PP
.RE
\fIdoc/tasks/future.\&tm.\&md\fR
.RS 4
Planned work not yet scheduled to a sprint.\&
.PP
.RE
\fIdoc/tasks/completed.\&tm.\&md\fR
.RS 4
Append\-only archive of completed sprints, newest first.\&
.PP
.RE
\fIdoc/tasks/archive/<YYYY>/<YYYY\-MM>.\&tm.\&md\fR
.RS 4
Sections aged out of \fIcompleted.\&tm.\&md\fR.\& Tool\-managed; never
hand\-authored, and never rewritten once written.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration uses the same flat `key: value` subset as frontmatter, read
from two locations, each optional:
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fBGlobal\fR — \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/taskmark/config\fR, falling back to
\fI\(ti/.\&config/taskmark/config\fR when unset.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBLocal\fR — \fI.\&taskmarkrc\fR in the directory \fBtm\fR is invoked from.\&
.PD
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
tasks_dir: doc/tasks
active_file: active\&.tm\&.md
future_file: future\&.tm\&.md
completed_file: completed\&.tm\&.md
archive_dir: archive
.fi
.RE
.PP
Resolution is per key, highest priority first: an explicit command\-line
option, the local file, the global file, then the built\-in default shown
above.\& An absent file, an absent key, or an unparseable line falls back
silently to the next source.\& See \fIdoc/taskmark_spec.\&md\fR §10 for the full
resolution order and the additional hub\-related keys.\&
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
\fIdoc/taskmark_spec.\&md\fR
.RS 4
The SPEC\-TASKMARK\-03 specification implemented by this tool.\&
.RE
